virglrenderer: new Venus devices wait after the Mac's driver loses one

What: when the Mac's Vulkan driver answers VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST to a VM's
Venus work (vkQueueSubmit/2, the fence and timeline semaphore waits and
queries, vkr's own sync submit and fence thread, vkDeviceWaitIdle at
teardown), vkr counts a lost device and refuses vkCreateDevice for a while
(VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED, one log line naming the app and the wait):
10 s after the first, doubling for each further one within 30 min, at most
10 min; reports within 2 s of the last counted one are the same loss.
Devices that exist go on. One state per QEMU process (one VM), under a
mutex; the rules are src/venus/vkr_restart_guard.h, without vkr.
Why: an app in the VM that a harness or a service starts again and again
after each lost device went straight back to the Mac's driver every time.
A short, growing wait between rounds keeps that loop from hammering the
driver; apps that do not lose devices never see it.
Upstream: OmacVM policy, not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-restart-guard.sh (CI and the runtime build:
the header's rules on the CPU).

